  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "David Grusch, a former US intelligence officer who went public as a whistleblower, says the strange objects of the 1950s were basically the same thing pilots report now. He points to reports from the Air Force Office of Special Investigations (OSI), the Air Force's own investigative branch, that described what looked like flying butane tanks, and tells Michels that \"the tic tac of today was the flying butane tank photo of the 1950s.\" The Tic Tac is a white oval object, shaped like the mint, that Navy pilots have described, so his point is that the same kind of craft has been seen, and filed away, for decades."
